# snd03-card.list -- what tools/sync-card.sh puts onto the owner's Pi card for the SND03 hardware probe.
# Format: tools/sync-card.sh header. The probe is the kernel itself; it needs no program, no file and no change
# to cmdline.txt or config.txt. So this list names no file: the kernel comes through
#   --kernels <run>/kernels --active kerns03.img
# (BOOT:kerns03.img + BOOT:kernel8.img; the card's old kernel8.img is saved to card-before/ first), built after
# the change has landed with
#   tools/sync-card.sh kernels <agent scratch>/kernels kerns03.img=snd-probe
# and copied to measurements/measurement-2026-11-12-snd03/kernels/ (KERNELS.TXT records commit and dirty flags).
# Optional, not needed: `serial=on` in cmdline.txt puts the same text on the serial line (GPIO 14/15).
# The probe writes no drive. After the run the old kernel8.img goes back from card-before/.
